@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Compendium</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h1>About Compendium</h1>
    <p class="lead">An OKF-first knowledge catalog for enterprise knowledge</p>

    <div class="row mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">What is Compendium?</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>
                        Compendium helps enterprise architects connect AI agents to the documents their
                        organization already has — scattered across SharePoint sites, Confluence spaces,
                        wikis, and shared drives — and turn them into a living, agent-curated map of
                        the business.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Most enterprise knowledge already exists, written for humans skimming a page.
                        Compendium's job is to turn that sprawl into a single, coherent knowledge catalog:
                        a directory of interlinked concepts describing the enterprise's architecture,
                        systems, business processes, and integrations.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Open Knowledge Format (OKF)</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>
                        Compendium is <strong>OKF-first</strong>: every concept it produces is a plain
                        markdown file with YAML frontmatter, conforming to the
                        <a href="https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md" target="_blank">
                            Open Knowledge Format
                        </a>.
                    </p>
                    <p>This means the catalog is:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Readable without Compendium</strong> — Browse in Obsidian, a static file server, or hand to any LLM as context</li>
                        <li><strong>Version-controlled</strong> — Lives in git with diffs, blame, and pull requests</li>
                        <li><strong>Portable</strong> — No proprietary store between you and your metadata</li>
                        <li><strong>Trustable at scale</strong> — Provenance, trust, and lifecycle fields let an agent-maintained corpus stay honest</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Key Features</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h6>Connectors</h6>
                    <p>Connect to existing knowledge sources:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>SharePoint sites</li>
                        <li>Confluence spaces</li>
                        <li>Markdown wikis</li>
                        <li>Local file systems</li>
                        <li>Git repositories</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h6 class="mt-3">Supported Formats</h6>
                    <p>Ingest from 14+ file formats:</p>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <ul>
                                <li>Documents: .txt, .md, .pdf, .docx</li>
                                <li>Data: .json, .xml, .csv, .xlsx</li>
                                <li>Email: .eml, .msg, .ost</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <ul>
                                <li>Diagrams: .drawio, .vsdx</li>
                                <li>Architecture: .archimate</li>
                                <li>Data Maps: Excel/CSV lineage tracking</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h6 class="mt-3">AI Agent</h6>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Curate</strong> — Ingest documents, create concepts, link relationships, flag stale knowledge</li>
                        <li><strong>Answer</strong> — Field questions grounded in the catalog with traceable sources</li>
                        <li><strong>Search</strong> — Find concepts across the entire knowledge base</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Data Map Support</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>
                        Compendium includes specialized support for <strong>data lineage tracking</strong>
                        through data maps. Document field-level flows from source systems to destinations:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Automatic detection of data map file format</li>
                        <li>Groups field mappings by integration name</li>
                        <li>Tracks source and destination systems</li>
                        <li>Categorizes destination types (Database, File, Email, API, etc.)</li>
                        <li>Preserves transformation logic and business rules</li>
                        <li>Enables graph-based lineage queries</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Version</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <dl class="mb-0">
                        <dt>Version:</dt>
                        <dd>0.1.0-alpha</dd>

                        <dt>Status:</dt>
                        <dd><span class="badge bg-warning">Early Preview</span></dd>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header">
